<description>
Extend the existing horizontal color pattern to twice the input width.

Input structure
- The grid has a black background and one or more non-background rows.
- Every column belongs to a repeating horizontal period that may be truncated
  at the right edge of the input.
Rule
- Find the shortest horizontal period that explains all input rows.
- Keep the height fixed and continue that period until the grid is twice as
  wide as the input.
Key insight
- The output is not a copy of the input appended to itself; it is the next
  columns of the underlying periodic tile.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "the input grid as the visible prefix of a horizontally periodic tile",
  "transform": "find the shortest column period that explains all rows, then continue that period to twice the input width",
  "grid_shape": "same height as input; width doubled"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    height: 5 [observed]
    width: 6-9 (must be >= 2 * period so at least 2 full repeats are visible)
  tile:
    description: a column tile of width=period that repeats horizontally across the grid
    period: 2-4 (minimal -- tile must NOT itself be periodic)
    non_black_rows: 1-2 contiguous rows; remaining rows are all black [observed]
    colors: exactly 2 distinct non-black colors per tile [observed]
    constraint: each non-black tile row must use >=2 colors (not a single color repeated)
  pattern:
    input columns are tile columns taken mod period, possibly truncated at right edge
    black rows extend across full width (period is determined by non-black rows only)
  output:
    same height; width = 2 * input_width
    columns are tile columns mod period, extended to the doubled width
    first half equals the input verbatim

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is the constrained object; output is deterministic)
  steps:
    1. Pick height (5 observed, can vary 3-7 for diversity), width W in [6, 9], period P in [2, 4] with W >= 2*P
    2. Pick 1-2 contiguous non-black row indices within [0, height)
    3. Pick 2 distinct non-black colors
    4. Build a P-wide tile column; for each non-black row, fill P cells using the 2 colors ensuring each row uses both colors and the tile has no sub-period
    5. Tile the pattern to width W using col % P to get the input grid; set remaining rows to black
    6. Output is the same tile extended to width 2*W
  validation: verify _minimal_horizontal_period(input) == P (rejects degenerate sub-periodic tiles)
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

